# Laraplate Specific (caveman)

- App is modular Laravel (`nwidart/laravel-modules`).
- Core is foundation, loaded first, reused by all.
- CMS/ERP/AI/MES build on Core contracts and services.

- Module rules:
  - Keep module self-contained.
  - Keep dependency explicit in `module.json`.
  - Respect load priority.
  - Do not duplicate shared Core logic.
  - Table names prefixed by lowercase module name

- Stack baseline:
  - Laravel 12, PHP 8.5+, Filament, Sanctum, Pest.
  - Queue for heavy async jobs.
  - Eloquent-first, API-ready, test-first mindset.

- Global ecosystem details in `laravel-boost.mdc`.

- Eloquent model traits (IDE / PHPStan):
  - Use `@phpstan-require-extends \Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\Model` on traits meant for Eloquent models.
  - Do not use `@mixin Model` on traits (duplicate API across traits, IDE conflicts).
  - Do **not** add `@mixin IdeHelper{Model}` to models. `_ide_helper_models.php` is gitignored and outside PHPStan's `paths`, so every such tag is a `class.notFound` error (177 of them, 2026-09-17) and buys nothing back. `post_migrate` runs `ide-helper:models -N`: generated docblocks go to the helper file, model files are left alone. `EloquentMixinModelHook`, which completed those tags, is deleted for the same reason.
  - If the IDE link is ever wanted back, it costs more than the tags: `_ide_helper_models.php` must be generated before every analysis and declared in PHPStan's `scanFiles`. Measured gain when it was tried: 674 -> 591 errors on `Modules/Core/app/Models`.
  - Add `@property` on the trait only for host-specific fields the trait reads (not the full Model API).
  - Factory/command traits that are not used on models must not declare `require-extends Model`.

- Pint `final_class`:
  - Keep `final_class: false` in every `pint.json` (root + modules). Never enable it globally.
  - Leaf Eloquent models should stay `final` manually; Pint cannot know which classes are extended by the host app.
  - `Modules\Core\Models\User` must remain non-`final` because `App\Models\User` extends it.
